From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: drm/msm/dp: read the EDID on every connector probe

The bridge advertises DRM_BRIDGE_OP_MODES and answers .get_modes from the
copy of the EDID taken when the sink was plugged, so a sink that changes
its EDID while it stays connected keeps being described by the modes it
first reported, and a probe forced from userspace returns the same stale
list. Advertise DRM_BRIDGE_OP_EDID and read the EDID over DDC from
.edid_read instead, which is what the bridge connector helper calls on
every probe and what the other bridges already do. A read that fails
hands out a copy of the EDID taken at plug time, so a transient DDC error
cannot empty the mode list of a display that is still lit.

That leaves msm_dp_display_get_modes() and msm_dp_panel_get_modes()
without a caller, so drop them and their declarations.

Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 31 +++++++---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.h |  3 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_drm.c     | 30 +++------
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c   | 14 -----
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.h   |  2 -
 5 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 48 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -739,19 +739,34 @@ enum drm_mode_status msm_dp_bridge_mode_valid(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	return MODE_OK;
 }
 
-int msm_dp_display_get_modes(struct msm_dp *dp)
+const struct drm_edid *msm_dp_display_edid_read(struct msm_dp *dp,
+						struct drm_connector *connector)
 {
-	struct msm_dp_display_private *msm_dp_display;
+	struct msm_dp_display_private *priv =
+		container_of(dp, struct msm_dp_display_private, msm_dp_display);
+	const struct drm_edid *drm_edid;
+	int ret;
 
-	if (!dp) {
-		DRM_ERROR("invalid params\n");
-		return 0;
+	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&dp->pdev->dev);
+	if (ret) {
+		DRM_ERROR("failed to pm_runtime_resume\n");
+		goto cached;
 	}
 
-	msm_dp_display = container_of(dp, struct msm_dp_display_private, msm_dp_display);
+	drm_edid = drm_edid_read_ddc(connector, &priv->aux->ddc);
+
+	pm_runtime_put_sync(&dp->pdev->dev);
 
-	return msm_dp_panel_get_modes(msm_dp_display->panel,
-		dp->connector);
+	if (drm_edid)
+		return drm_edid;
+
+cached:
+	/*
+	 * A transient DDC failure must not empty the mode list of a display
+	 * that is still lit, so hand out a copy of what the sink reported when
+	 * it was plugged instead.
+	 */
+	return priv->panel->drm_edid ? drm_edid_dup(priv->panel->drm_edid) : NULL;
 }
 
 bool msm_dp_display_check_video_test(struct msm_dp *dp)
